    "description": "Deals have no planned end date. The end date is only recorded when a deal is shut down.\n\n=== IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS ===\n\n* Remove Effective End Date as a list-view column. Keep the field on the record page.\n\n* Rename the Effective Start Date list-view column to just 'Effective'. SIDE EFFECT already flagged to Joyce: renaming the field label changes it everywhere, so the record page will read 'Effective' and 'Effective End Date'. Joyce: 'that's fine. I just didn't want effective end date as a column in the list view.'\n\n* Business rule, Joyce: 'really there isn't an end date until we shut down the deal... I would just like have it as a field that saves against the deal record when we close off the deal.'\n\n* Note: Effective Start Date is now also the SORT field on the Deals related lists (BUILD-132).\n\n=== OPEN QUESTIONS ===\n\n* Automation was implied but never committed. 'saves against the deal record when we close off the deal' sounds like an auto-stamp when Deal Status flips to Closed/Inactive, but nobody agreed to build it. Auto-stamp (separate story per convention), or manual entry at close?\n\n=== SOURCE ===\n\n* Aug 11 call — Joyce 45:03-46:47\n\n* Aug 17 call — sort field decision\n\nDependencies: None\n\nOwner (proposed): TBD\n\nRemember to update the requirements documentation as part of this change.\n\nCreated 2026-08-17 from the Operator/Partner ticket review, approved by Kobi.",
